gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.002424693486675928,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":47.4,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.2699607594978496,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":37.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.05757004563965712,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.08797902786921774,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":4.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.12119973420272756,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":85.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02930365911878859,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":43.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.022493038008158273,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":21.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.018237891721027147,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":69.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.033469997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":22.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bar Harbor Bankshares operates as the holding company for Bar Harbor Bank & Trust that provides banking and nonbanking products and services primarily to consumers and businesses. The company offers deposit products, including interest-bearing and non-interest-bearing demand accounts, savings accounts, time deposits, and money market deposit accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. It also provides commercial construction loans, such as raw land, land development, and construction of commercial and multifamily residential properties; commercial real estate owner occupied and non-owner occupied loans; tax exempt loans to various state and municipal government entities; commercial and industrial loans, including loans for the purpose of financing working capital and capital investment; residential real estate loans consists of one-to-four family homes; home equity loans; and consumer loans, including personal lines of credit and amortizing loans to qualified individuals for various purposes, such as auto loans, recreational equipment, overdraft protection, and other consumer loans, as well as allowance for credit losses. In addition, the company provides life insurance, annuity, and retirement products; financial planning services; and third-party investment and insurance services. Further, it offers trust and estate administration, wealth advisory, and investment management services to individuals, businesses, not-for-profit organizations, and municipalities; and 401(K) plan, financial, estate and charitable planning, investment management, family office, municipal, and tax services. Bar Harbor Bankshares was founded in 1887 and is headquartered in Bar Harbor, Maine.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Curtis C. Simard | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 530 people. Revenue per employee of $319K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $82K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Bar Harbor Bankshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $696M market cap on $169M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $43M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.31\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.19082939986513925},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 17% margin of safety against estimated fair value","28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of BHB and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/38/Behavioral_Patterns_of_BHB_and_Institutional_Flows_111026030803_1794298083.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794298083.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(BHB) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/BHB_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_103126040001_1793433601.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793433601.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bar Harbor Bankshares Director Lauri E. Fernald Granted 966 Shares of Restricted Stock","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/bar-harbor-bankshares-director-lauri-e-fernald-granted-966-shares-of-restricted-stock","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586685.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bar Harbor Bankshares Director Heather D. Jones Acquires 966 Shares in November 2026 Stock Grant","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/a